    "intro_html":  "Escondidinho means little hidden thing, and the hidden thing is the meat. Seasoned beef goes on the bottom, creamy mashed potato goes over it like a blanket, cheese goes on top, and it bakes until the whole surface blisters. Brazil makes this with catupiry, a soft tangy cheese that does not exist here, so cream cheese is the standard stand-in and it works. Cilantro through the beef is what keeps it from tasting like a British shepherd\u0027s pie with a tan.",
