    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003ePotatoes are the cheapest thing in this dish and they are half of it.\u003c/strong\u003e Buy the big bag and store them cool and dark, and the mash layer costs next to nothing.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eCream cheese replaces catupiry and is a fraction of the price of imported cheese.\u003c/strong\u003e Buy the store brand bricks, which behave identically once melted into a mash.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eShred the mozzarella from a block.\u003c/strong\u003e Bagged shreds are coated in anti-caking starch that keeps them from melting into the smooth sheet this topping wants.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eCilantro is what makes it Brazilian.\u003c/strong\u003e One bunch costs pocket change and it is the difference between this and a generic beef and potato bake."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Peel and boil the potatoes until they fall apart on a fork, then drain them well and let the steam escape for a minute.",
                    "Mash the potatoes with the milk, butter, parmesan cheese, salt, and black pepper until smooth, then set the mash aside.",
                    "Heat the olive oil in a large skillet and cook the diced yellow onion and garlic until softened.",
                    "Add the ground beef, break it up, and cook until browned with no pink remaining, then drain off the excess fat.",
                    "Stir in the chili powder, ground cumin, salt, and black pepper, then take the pan off the heat and fold in the cream cheese and the chopped cilantro until melted through.",
                    "Spread the beef in an even layer in a large baking dish and blanket it with the mashed potato.",
                    "Scatter the mozzarella over the top and bake at 400 degrees until melted, bubbling, and browned in spots."
                ],
